  "rules": [
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "level": "allow",
      "reason": "an edit on a branch reaches no one else until a merge"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "auth",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a mistake in sign-in or permissions lets the wrong person in"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "payments",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a mistake here moves money or changes a price"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "personal_data",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a mistake here exposes or changes data about people"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "secrets",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a mistake here leaks a key or weakens the cryptography"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "migrations",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a schema change can lose data and is hard to undo"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "module_boundaries",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "the rules that keep modules apart change, so a person hears of it"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "ci",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "what builds, tests, and ships the code changes, so a person hears of it"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "infra",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "what runs the service changes, so a person hears of it"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "dependencies",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "third-party code enters the build, so a person hears of it"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "agent_config",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "what agents read changes how they work, so a person hears of it"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "project_config",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "the project's own settings change, so a person hears of it"
    },
    {
      "action": "code.edit",
      "area": "risk_rules",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a change to what makes an agent ask is the person's to make"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.commit",
      "level": "allow",
      "reason": "a commit stays on this machine and is easy to undo"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.push",
      "branch": "own",
      "level": "allow",
      "reason": "your own branch is yours, and a push there lands nothing on the default branch"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.push",
      "branch": "default",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a push to the default branch reaches everyone with no review"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.push",
      "branch": "shared",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a push to a shared branch changes work that others build on"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.push.force",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a force push can erase commits that others have"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.history.rewrite",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a rewrite can lose work, and every clone with the old commits must repair"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.branch.delete",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a deleted branch can take unmerged work with it"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.tag.create",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a tag can mark or move a release, which a person decides"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.merge",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a merge into the default or a shared branch lands work that others use"
    },
    {
      "action": "git.merge",
      "branch": "own",
      "level": "allow",
      "reason": "a merge into your own branch lands nothing on the default branch"
    },
    {
      "action": "pr.open",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "a pull request is public to the team, and nothing merges until a person says so"
    },
    {
      "action": "pr.merge",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a merge lands the change on its base branch"
    },
    {
      "action": "workflow.run",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "a run spends CI time and can act on the repository, so a person hears of it"
    },
    {
      "action": "dependency.add",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "a new package runs its own code when it installs, so a person hears of it, and a delegation leaves it to them"
    },
    {
      "action": "network.listen",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "a listener lets other devices on the network reach this machine"
    },
    {
      "action": "commit_status.post",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a check's result is CI's to report, never an agent's"
    },
    {
      "action": "branch_protection.change",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "branch protection is the control that holds whatever an agent runs"
    },
    {
      "action": "repo.settings.change",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a repository's settings decide who sees it and who can change it"
    },
    {
      "action": "intent.agree",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "Intent agreement is a person's decision on what the work sets out to do"
    },
    {
      "action": "spec.approve",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "Spec approval is a person's decision on what gets built"
    },
    {
      "action": "spec.revise",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a change to a frozen test or the Acceptance changes what the approval covered"
    },
    {
      "action": "deploy.run",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a deploy changes what people use"
    },
    {
      "action": "records.push",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a pushed record is permanent, and everyone who reads the repository reads it"
    },
    {
      "action": "release.publish",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a release reaches every user and cannot be taken back"
    },
    {
      "action": "migration.run",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a migration changes a database that other people use"
    },
    {
      "action": "migration.run.local",
      "level": "report",
      "reason": "a database only this checkout uses holds no one else's data"
    },
    {
      "action": "migration.rollback",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a rollback loses the data the reversed steps held"
    },
    {
      "action": "infra.apply",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "applying infrastructure changes what runs, and can destroy it"
    },
    {
      "action": "data.delete",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "deleted data may not come back"
    },
    {
      "action": "data.production.access",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "production data belongs to the people it describes"
    },
    {
      "action": "secret.use",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a secret in the session can leak through any output"
    },
    {
      "action": "message.send",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "a message reaches people and cannot be unsent"
    },
    {
      "action": "money.spend",
      "level": "ask",
      "reason": "spending money is the person's decision"
    }
  ],
  "delegation": {
    "description": "What a standing delegation may let the `aidd-team:delegate` role answer, and what `aidd delegate check` reads to decide it may (docs/METHOD.md, \"A standing delegation\"). Only these actions are delegable, each in its exact command template, where `<name>` is a value the check reads. Every other action is reserved: always the person's. A config's `delegation` block picks from these and can only narrow them.",
    "actions": {
      "spec.approve": {
        "since": "1.0.0",
        "description": "Approve a ready Spec whose new tests fail on the base, on the solo profile for the major route."
      },
      "git.push": {
        "since": "1.0.0",
        "template": [
          "git",
          "push",
          "origin",
          "<sha>:refs/heads/<branch>"
        ],
        "description": "Push the change's own branch: the head branch of its open pull request into the default branch, with no force."
      },
      "git.merge": {
        "since": "1.0.0",
        "template": [
          "git",
          "merge",
          "--no-ff",
          "-m",
          "<message>",
          "<sha>"
        ],
        "description": "Merge the change into the default branch on this machine, on the solo profile with no remote, once the check ran the suite on the head itself."
      },
      "pr.merge": {
        "since": "1.0.0",
        "template": [
          "gh",
          "pr",
          "merge",
          "<number>",
          "--repo",
          "<repo>",
          "<method>",
          "--match-head-commit",
          "<sha>",
          "--body",
          "<message>"
        ],
        "description": "Merge a pull request into the default branch on GitHub, at its exact head, once the `tests` check passed there."
      }
    },
    "reserved_areas": [
      "module_boundaries",
      "ci",
      "dependencies",
      "agent_config",
      "risk_rules",
      "project_config"
    ],
    "rises_to_ask": [
      "dependency.add",
      "migration.run.local"
    ],
    "test_paths": [
